-- title:
--   Point congruent to the counit on a formally étale level is trivial
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p$ with $K$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let $\mathcal{O}_K$ denote [`PadicAlgCl.ringOfIntegers p K`](def/PadicAlgCl_RingOfIntegers.html#L11), the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ obtained by intersecting the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ with $K$. Let $h$ be a natural number and let $Q$ be a $p$-divisible group over $\mathcal{O}_K$ of height data $(p,h)$ in the project's sense: a family of commutative rings $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ ($v \in \mathbb{N}$), each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathcal{O}_K$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}_K$-module of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra-algebra maps $Q.\mathrm{transition}\,v : Q.\mathrm{level}(v+1) \to Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$ in the Hopf-algebra sense. Fix a level $v$ such that $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ is formally étale over $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $g$ be a point of $Q$ of level $v$ with values in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$, that is, an element of the convolution group of $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebra homomorphisms $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$. Assume that for every $a \in Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ one has $\|g(a) - \varepsilon(a)\| < 1$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit of the Hopf algebra, its value taken in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ via $\mathcal{O}_K \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$. Then $g$ is the identity of the convolution group, i.e. the unit point.
--
--   This is the injectivity of reduction on the points of an étale level of a $p$-divisible group: a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$-point lying in the kernel of reduction is the unit section. It is used in the analysis of the action of inertia on points, in [`PDivisibleGroup.forall_dual_apply_eq_zero_of_forall_norm_sub_counit_lt_one_of_forall_inertia_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.forall_dual_apply_eq_zero_of_forall_norm_sub_counit_lt_one_of_forall_inertia_of_ringOfIntegers).
